1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,610
At six-oh-two in the morning my phone made a sound I had never heard before.

2
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:06,197
Not a ringtone.

3
00:00:06,547 --> 00:00:07,562
An alarm.

4
00:00:08,462 --> 00:00:10,767
The screen said: emergency alert.

5
00:00:11,117 --> 00:00:12,353
Remain calm.

6
00:00:12,703 --> 00:00:14,956
Next update in twenty-four hours.

7
00:00:15,856 --> 00:00:17,731
I read the last line twice.

8
00:00:18,081 --> 00:00:19,526
Twenty-four hours.

9
00:00:19,876 --> 00:00:23,469
Whoever wrote it did not think I would need to know anything sooner.

10
00:00:24,369 --> 00:00:25,853
I walked to the window.

11
00:00:26,203 --> 00:00:30,500
Down on the street, a man ran past a stopped car with his shoes in his hand.

12
00:00:30,850 --> 00:00:32,816
A woman was screaming a name.

13
00:00:33,166 --> 00:00:37,033
Someone was leaning on a horn, and nobody was telling him to stop.

14
00:00:37,383 --> 00:00:43,984
At the far end of the block, a few people were walking toward the crowd, slowly, in a way that made the crowd run faster.

15
00:00:44,884 --> 00:00:47,371
I did not understand what I was looking at.

16
00:00:47,721 --> 00:00:50,299
I only understood that I could not stay here.

17
00:00:50,649 --> 00:00:52,576
The building was already loud.

18
00:00:52,926 --> 00:00:55,738
Doors, footsteps, voices in the stairwell.

19
00:00:56,088 --> 00:00:59,356
Noise, I would learn, is the one thing you cannot afford.

20
00:01:00,256 --> 00:01:01,571
I packed fast.

21
00:01:01,921 --> 00:01:03,496
Two bottles of water.

22
00:01:03,846 --> 00:01:05,213
Two snack bars.

23
00:01:05,563 --> 00:01:06,735
My flashlight.

24
00:01:07,085 --> 00:01:09,272
My phone, at eighty-five percent.

25
00:01:09,622 --> 00:01:14,518
I took the small backpack from the hook by the door, and I did not look back at the apartment.

26
00:01:15,418 --> 00:01:17,787
That was the first decision of the day.

27
00:01:18,137 --> 00:01:19,804
It was not a good one yet.

28
00:01:20,154 --> 00:01:21,625
But it was a decision.

29
00:01:22,525 --> 00:01:24,009
The clock had started.

30
00:01:24,909 --> 00:01:28,919
Everyone on the street was running the same way, so I ran the same way.

31
00:01:29,269 --> 00:01:30,415
Toward the mall.

32
00:01:31,315 --> 00:01:34,557
It had big doors, bright lights, security guards.

33
00:01:34,907 --> 00:01:37,524
It looked like the kind of place that would be safe.

34
00:01:37,874 --> 00:01:40,790
That is exactly why everybody was going there.

35
00:01:41,690 --> 00:01:43,383
The entrance was a funnel.

36
00:01:43,733 --> 00:01:47,977
Hundreds of people pushing through two doors, and the noise bouncing off the glass.

37
00:01:48,327 --> 00:01:50,215
I told myself it was fine.

38
00:01:50,565 --> 00:01:51,984
Crowds mean help.

39
00:01:52,334 --> 00:01:54,404
Crowds mean someone is in charge.

40
00:01:55,304 --> 00:01:57,088
Inside, it got worse.

41
00:01:57,438 --> 00:02:00,979
A man shouted for everyone to stay calm, and nobody listened.

42
00:02:01,329 --> 00:02:03,673
A child was crying somewhere above me.

43
00:02:04,023 --> 00:02:08,098
I found a small kiosk with its shutter half open and took what I could carry.

44
00:02:08,448 --> 00:02:10,023
Two bottles of water.

45
00:02:10,373 --> 00:02:11,910
Three cans of food.

46
00:02:12,810 --> 00:02:15,309
I did not check how many exits there were.

47
00:02:15,659 --> 00:02:17,964
I did not look for a quiet corner.

48
00:02:18,314 --> 00:02:20,189
I did what everyone else did.

49
00:02:20,539 --> 00:02:21,945
I followed the noise.

50
00:02:22,845 --> 00:02:24,433
Here is what I got wrong.

51
00:02:24,783 --> 00:02:26,762
I thought a crowd was protection.

52
00:02:27,112 --> 00:02:28,661
A crowd is a signal.

53
00:02:29,011 --> 00:02:34,102
Every shout, every alarm, every breaking glass door was telling them exactly where we were.

54
00:02:35,002 --> 00:02:36,955
It started on the upper level.

55
00:02:37,305 --> 00:02:38,607
I never saw how.

56
00:02:38,957 --> 00:02:45,050
First a scream, then a surge, and then the whole floor was moving at once toward the only place anyone could think of.

57
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:46,546
The stairwell.

58
00:02:47,446 --> 00:02:48,761
I got swept in.

59
00:02:49,111 --> 00:02:52,197
The stairs were too narrow for the number of people on them.

60
00:02:52,547 --> 00:02:56,843
Shoulders, elbows, bags, and a metal handrail running down the middle.

61
00:02:57,193 --> 00:02:58,860
My backpack caught on it.

62
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:02,976
For a moment I did not understand why I had stopped moving.

63
00:03:03,326 --> 00:03:07,245
The crowd kept pushing, and the strap held me to the railing like a hand.

64
00:03:07,595 --> 00:03:08,883
I pulled once.

65
00:03:09,233 --> 00:03:10,054
Nothing.

66
00:03:10,404 --> 00:03:12,343
People were shouting behind me.

67
00:03:12,693 --> 00:03:14,021
Someone fell.

68
00:03:14,371 --> 00:03:17,900
Below us the sound changed, and I knew what it meant without looking.

69
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:23,904
I slipped one arm out of the strap, dragged the bag free, and tore my palm open on the metal.

70
00:03:24,254 --> 00:03:25,256
It stung.

71
00:03:25,606 --> 00:03:26,960
I did not care.

72
00:03:27,860 --> 00:03:31,271
At the next landing there was a grey door with three words on it.

73
00:03:31,621 --> 00:03:32,832
Staff only.

74
00:03:33,732 --> 00:03:34,943
It was unlocked.

75
00:03:35,293 --> 00:03:37,766
I pushed through and pulled it shut behind me.

76
00:03:38,116 --> 00:03:41,345
A corridor, cold air, the smell of cleaning fluid.

77
00:03:41,695 --> 00:03:43,830
Through the wall I could hear the mall.

78
00:03:44,180 --> 00:03:50,430
I went the other way, down a ramp, through a second door, and out onto a loading dock where the morning was suddenly quiet.

79
00:03:51,330 --> 00:03:55,497
I sat down between two dumpsters, and I realised my hand was shaking.

80
00:03:56,397 --> 00:03:59,730
I did not know how long I could stay there, so I used the time.

81
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:05,626
I opened the notes on my phone and typed with one thumb, because my other hand was bleeding onto my sleeve.

82
00:04:06,526 --> 00:04:07,529
Rule one.

83
00:04:07,879 --> 00:04:09,102
Noise draws them.

84
00:04:09,452 --> 00:04:10,533
Be quiet.

85
00:04:11,433 --> 00:04:12,513
Rule two.

86
00:04:12,863 --> 00:04:15,702
Never go into a place without a second way out.

87
00:04:16,602 --> 00:04:17,747
Rule three.

88
00:04:18,097 --> 00:04:21,183
Do not stay anywhere you cannot leave in under a minute.

89
00:04:22,083 --> 00:04:24,583
Two percent of my battery for three lines.

90
00:04:24,933 --> 00:04:26,157
It was worth it.

91
00:04:27,057 --> 00:04:30,325
From behind the dumpster I could see a long stretch of street.

92
00:04:30,675 --> 00:04:37,094
Somewhere in the mall an alarm was ringing and ringing, and the people left out here were drifting toward it, one after another.

93
00:04:37,444 --> 00:04:38,746
They did not run.

94
00:04:39,096 --> 00:04:40,684
They did not look for me.

95
00:04:41,034 --> 00:04:44,224
They walked toward the sound the way water finds a low place.

96
00:04:45,124 --> 00:04:47,324
That was when I understood the rest.

97
00:04:47,674 --> 00:04:49,119
They were not fast.

98
00:04:49,469 --> 00:04:50,901
They were not clever.

99
00:04:51,251 --> 00:04:52,722
They followed the noise.

100
00:04:53,072 --> 00:04:57,291
And if I could be quiet, and far enough away, they would not follow me at all.

101
00:04:58,191 --> 00:05:00,769
By the afternoon I needed somewhere to rest.

102
00:05:01,119 --> 00:05:05,298
The streets had gone quiet the way a place does when everyone has left in a hurry.

103
00:05:05,648 --> 00:05:07,836
At the end of a row I found a house.

104
00:05:08,186 --> 00:05:10,607
The front door stood open a hand's width.

105
00:05:10,957 --> 00:05:11,999
No lights.

106
00:05:12,349 --> 00:05:14,067
It looked like what I wanted.

107
00:05:14,417 --> 00:05:15,250
A bed.

108
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:16,459
A lock.

109
00:05:16,809 --> 00:05:17,942
A back door.

110
00:05:18,842 --> 00:05:20,326
Then I saw the frame.

111
00:05:20,676 --> 00:05:24,895
The wood around the lock was splintered, and the splinters pointed out, not in.

112
00:05:25,245 --> 00:05:27,575
Whatever broke that door had been inside.

113
00:05:28,475 --> 00:05:30,402
I stood there for a long time.

114
00:05:30,752 --> 00:05:32,262
Then the handle moved.

115
00:05:32,612 --> 00:05:33,562
Slowly.

116
00:05:33,912 --> 00:05:35,423
Down, and back up.

117
00:05:35,773 --> 00:05:37,556
Nobody opened the door.

118
00:05:38,456 --> 00:05:42,636
Above me, in the upstairs window, a shadow crossed the glass and was gone.

119
00:05:43,536 --> 00:05:44,851
I did not run.

120
00:05:45,201 --> 00:05:46,203
Rule one.

121
00:05:46,553 --> 00:05:53,597
I took one step back, then another, and I walked away with my hands tight on the straps of my backpack until the house was behind a hedge.

122
00:05:53,947 --> 00:05:56,837
My heart was going so hard I thought it could be heard.

123
00:05:57,187 --> 00:05:58,307
It could not.

124
00:05:59,207 --> 00:06:03,217
That was the second decision of the day, and it was better than the first.

125
00:06:04,117 --> 00:06:06,213
The light was already going orange.

126
00:06:06,563 --> 00:06:08,126
I had maybe an hour.

127
00:06:08,476 --> 00:06:11,561
I made myself stop and think like the notes on my phone.

128
00:06:12,461 --> 00:06:14,766
The first place was a parking garage.

129
00:06:15,116 --> 00:06:17,850
Open on every side, concrete, echoing.

130
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:19,710
Too many entrances.

131
00:06:20,060 --> 00:06:20,854
No.

132
00:06:21,754 --> 00:06:23,941
The second was an apartment block.

133
00:06:24,291 --> 00:06:26,335
Six floors, one stairwell.

134
00:06:26,685 --> 00:06:29,459
I had just spent the morning inside a stairwell.

135
00:06:29,809 --> 00:06:30,603
No.

136
00:06:31,503 --> 00:06:35,109
The third was a small utility building behind a row of shops.

137
00:06:35,459 --> 00:06:37,386
One steel door at the front.

138
00:06:37,736 --> 00:06:39,754
A narrow service hatch at the back.

139
00:06:40,104 --> 00:06:41,302
No windows.

140
00:06:41,652 --> 00:06:43,930
It was cold, and it smelled of oil.

141
00:06:44,280 --> 00:06:48,577
It had no water, no bed, nothing a normal person would call comfortable.

142
00:06:48,927 --> 00:06:51,479
But it had two ways out, and it was quiet.

143
00:06:52,379 --> 00:06:54,631
I stood at the steel door and listened.

144
00:06:54,981 --> 00:06:55,801
Nothing.

145
00:06:56,151 --> 00:06:59,042
I counted slowly to sixty and listened again.

146
00:06:59,392 --> 00:07:00,212
Nothing.

147
00:07:01,112 --> 00:07:05,330
Then I went in, and I closed the door as softly as I have ever closed anything.

148
00:07:06,230 --> 00:07:07,623
Night came fast.

149
00:07:07,973 --> 00:07:11,059
With the power gone, the city went completely dark.

150
00:07:11,409 --> 00:07:13,753
I did not use the flashlight at first.

151
00:07:14,103 --> 00:07:15,535
Light draws them too.

152
00:07:15,885 --> 00:07:20,585
I sat with my back to the wall opposite the door and the hatch at my shoulder, and I waited.

153
00:07:21,485 --> 00:07:23,230
Around midnight I heard it.

154
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:24,960
A scrape outside.

155
00:07:25,310 --> 00:07:26,403
Then another.

156
00:07:26,753 --> 00:07:29,253
Something dragging a foot across concrete.

157
00:07:30,153 --> 00:07:35,218
I switched the flashlight on for ten seconds, only to see the room, and turned it off again.

158
00:07:35,568 --> 00:07:37,807
In that moment the steel door moved.

159
00:07:38,157 --> 00:07:39,251
Not a knock.

160
00:07:39,601 --> 00:07:40,564
A push.

161
00:07:40,914 --> 00:07:41,773
Once.

162
00:07:42,123 --> 00:07:42,930
Twice.

163
00:07:43,280 --> 00:07:45,624
Then a slow rhythm of hands on metal.

164
00:07:46,524 --> 00:07:47,982
They could not open it.

165
00:07:48,332 --> 00:07:49,855
They did not know how.

166
00:07:50,205 --> 00:07:53,642
But they were there, and the door was not made to last forever.

167
00:07:54,542 --> 00:07:56,287
I crawled to the back hatch.

168
00:07:56,637 --> 00:08:00,243
I held the lever with one hand and pressed the other over my own mouth.

169
00:08:00,593 --> 00:08:03,171
The pushing went on for what felt like an hour.

170
00:08:03,521 --> 00:08:06,047
Then, little by little, it thinned out.

171
00:08:06,397 --> 00:08:07,608
A last scrape.

172
00:08:07,958 --> 00:08:09,064
Then nothing.

173
00:08:09,414 --> 00:08:11,042
They had lost the noise.

174
00:08:11,392 --> 00:08:13,787
They had forgotten there was anything here.

175
00:08:14,687 --> 00:08:16,002
I did not leave.

176
00:08:16,352 --> 00:08:19,112
I stayed on my knees at the hatch until it was light.

177
00:08:20,012 --> 00:08:22,356
That was the third decision of the day.

178
00:08:22,706 --> 00:08:24,203
To do nothing at all.

179
00:08:25,103 --> 00:08:26,691
Dawn came grey and slow.

180
00:08:27,041 --> 00:08:31,494
I opened the hatch a finger's width, looked at an empty yard, and closed it again.

181
00:08:31,844 --> 00:08:34,383
I had been awake for more than twenty hours.

182
00:08:34,733 --> 00:08:41,504
I had a little over a litre of water, three meals of food, a scraped hand, a phone at sixty-two percent, and three rules.

183
00:08:42,404 --> 00:08:43,653
My phone buzzed.

184
00:08:44,003 --> 00:08:45,162
A new message.

185
00:08:45,512 --> 00:08:46,553
Automated.

186
00:08:46,903 --> 00:08:47,776
Flat.

187
00:08:48,126 --> 00:08:49,636
Evacuation point.

188
00:08:49,986 --> 00:08:52,355
River Crossing Bridge, north bank.

189
00:08:52,705 --> 00:08:54,593
Cut-off, twelve noon today.

190
00:08:55,493 --> 00:08:57,042
I read it four times.

191
00:08:57,392 --> 00:08:59,436
I should have asked who was sending it.

192
00:08:59,786 --> 00:09:02,534
I should have asked how many other people had read it.

193
00:09:02,884 --> 00:09:05,488
Instead I did what a tired person does.

194
00:09:05,838 --> 00:09:07,491
I wanted it to be true.

195
00:09:08,391 --> 00:09:10,253
I counted my supplies again.

196
00:09:10,603 --> 00:09:11,996
I checked the street.

197
00:09:12,346 --> 00:09:17,332
I put the backpack on, I stepped out into the cold, and I started walking toward the river.
